  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Serve path",
      "items": [
        "A dashboard toggle shows on the next check: the client reads conditionally, then decides locally.",
        "Warm read = one indexed Environment row + one Redis GET. No flag, state, or rule query at all.",
        "Precedence: kill switch → rules by ascending priority → percentage rollout → default, sorted inside the evaluator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two trust levels, one dependency",
      "items": [
        "X-SDK-Key is checked first, so a request carrying both headers authenticates as the key, not the user.",
        "Bearer JWT: 15 min access, 7 day refresh, no revocation, every owned project, all mutations.",
        "SDK key: no expiry until revoked, hard 403 on project mismatch, read-only, /bootstrap and /evaluate only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Coherence and failure",
      "items": [
        "Environment.version is both the cache token and the weak ETag; a stale entry is a miss, never a stale read.",
        "A matching If-None-Match returns 304 before the body loads. X-Catalyst-Cache names the answering layer.",
        "Every Redis helper swallows errors and reports a miss: a cache outage is a slowdown, never a 500."
      ]
    }
  ]
